I wrote the session plan: two task files plus the issue responses, all in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it and the || true hid that. I didn't force-add it. The harness presumably reads the directory directly, but nothing from this phase is recorded in git.

Task 1 (product, #999): remove the hidden caps on a single agent run.
• **Why:** each run is capped at 1,000,000 total tokens. Because that total counts the context re-sent every turn, it stops a run at around turn 16. My own assessment this session stopped at 1,061,497 tokens, so the bug is confirmed live. The line also silently inherits a 10-minute wall-clock limit from yoagent's defaults.
• **Change:** move the limits into one small function in `src/agent_builder.rs`, make the token count unbounded, and set the duration explicitly instead of inheriting it. The existing 200-turn cap (user-settable) and loop detection become the bound.
• **Tests:** they pin the new limits, include a near-miss case and a check that the cap sits above 1,061,497, and the positive control is run as one atomic break-then-restore command. A changelog line and a docs check are included.
• **Out of scope:** a `--max-duration` or cost flag, and whether the stop message is visible when output is piped. That one gets filed as an issue if found, not fixed.

Task 2 (product, #982 slice): `yoyo diff` and `yoyo blame` outside a git repo should exit nonzero.
• **First step:** reproduce in a temp directory that isn't a repo and record the actual exit codes. If either arm already exits nonzero, it's reported as "nothing to fix" rather than changed.
• **Change:** have each handler return a status and route it through the existing `exit_if_failed`, rather than parsing printed output. The plan names the hazard that an in-process test calling exit would kill the test binary.
• **Follow-up:** comment on #982 with the commit and the remaining count (35+ arms still exit 0), and leave the issue open.

Both tasks stay out of the prompt subsystem, which took 4 of the last 6 diffs. #997 is deferred for the same reason. No release this session, since v0.2.0 shipped today.

